problems.problem:
Let $a_1, a_2, \ldots, a_{11}$ be integers. Prove that there exist numbers $b_1, b_2, \ldots, b_{11}$ such that:
• $b_i \in \{-1,0,1\}$ for all $i \in \{1, 2,\ldots, 11\}$;
• not all of the $b_i$ are zero;
• the number $N=a_1b_1+a_2b_2+\cdots+a_{11}b_{11}$ is divisible by $2024$.

Mugdho and Dipto play a game on a row of $n \geq 5$ squares numbered $1$ to $n$. At the beginning, a pebble is put on the first square, and then the players move alternately, Mugdho starting. In a move a player may:
• move the pebble one square to the right;
• move the pebble four squares to the right;
• move the pebble two squares to the left.
A move is allowed only if the pebble stays within the row. The player who moves the pebble to the last ($n$-th) square wins. Determine for which values of $n$ each of the players has a winning strategy.

There are several juice boxes, exactly one of which is poisoned, and you have $n$ guinea pigs to test the boxes. The testing happens as follows:
• in each round, each guinea pig may taste any number of juice boxes;
• conversely, a juice box may be tasted by any number of guinea pigs;
• after the round ends, every guinea pig that tasted the poisoned juice dies.
Suppose you have to find the poisoned juice box in at most $k$ rounds. What is the maximum number of juice boxes for which this is possible?
